Job Description

At Thermo Fisher Scientific, you’ll discover meaningful work that makes a positive impact on a global scale. Join our colleagues in bringing our Mission to life - enabling our customers to make the world healthier, cleaner and safer. We provide our teams with the resources needed to achieve individual career goals while taking science a step beyond through research, development and delivery of life-changing therapies. With clinical trials conducted in 100+ countries and ongoing development of novel frameworks for clinical research through our PPD clinical research portfolio, our work spans laboratory, digital and decentralized clinical trial services. Your determination to deliver quality and accuracy will improve health outcomes that people and communities depend on – now and in the future.

For our Central   FP&A   Team in Bulgaria, part of our   Financial Planning & Analysis department , we are currently hiring:

Senior   FP&A   Coordinator (Centralized Services)

On this role you will be primarily engaged across centralized end-to-end processes with focus on quality, consistency and control point across data entries and systems. Additionally, by leveraging Microsoft tools such as Excel, SharePoint and others ,   our team focuses on efficiency and optimization where possible.

Responsibilities:

- Oracle ERP set-up and maintenance of the PPM (Project Portfolio Management) module;

- Collect, review and upload project data in Oracle, implement various updates to the data   in the course of   a study , and review   internal processes for improvement opportunities.

- CA Clarity™ PPM (Project and Portfolio Management) System set up and maintenance activities;

- Financial Unit Grid building, consolidation and loading into Clarity system;

- Data integrity activities across various systems;

- Preparation of various reporting across different segments of the business (Consolidated, Sponsor, Region and Therapeutic area);

Your Profile:

- University degree in Finance/Accounting/Economics/Information Technology or related;

- 2+ years in a finance   role   preferably in a multinational environment;

- Fluency in English (written and spoken);

- Excel literacy;

- Detailed-oriented personality with analytical thinking and problem-solving attitude;

- Handle multiple assignments and meet tight deadlines while maintaining high quality of work;

- Service-minded attitude and ability to adapt to changes;

- Eagerness to work in a global team supporting various types of activities;

What   W e   O ffer:

- You will benefit from a learning and development program which will allow you to grow vertically or move horizontally in the company, to best reflect your skills and desired career path ;

- You will enjoy our flexible working culture with hybrid working opportunities   ( remote working   opportunities   can be considered following an individual review ) ;

- Additional medical plan: health and dental care (fully covered by the employer) ;

- Mutltisport card (partially covered by the employer) ;

- Paid annual leave of 25 days, with 1 additional day added for each year of service in the company (up to 5 in total) ;

Our Mission is to enable our customers to make the world healthier, cleaner and safer. Watch as our colleagues explain 5 reasons to work with us. As   one   team of 100,000+ colleagues, we share a common set of values - Integrity, Intensity, Innovation and Involvement - working together to accelerate research, solve complex scientific challenges, drive technological innovation and support patients in need. #StartYourStory with PPD, part of Thermo Fisher Scientific, where diverse experiences, backgrounds and perspectives are valued.
